<div class="note">Withheld for this artifact class (Validation incident assessment — nonproduction): lessons learned · production severity · corrective action commitments. every anomalous observation declares a non-production purpose — this artifact documents a validation scenario and must never resemble a production postmortem</div>




<div class="pmh">1 · Executive summary</div>


<section>
  <h2>Incident at a glance</h2>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">Where it happened</span><span class="v">Not localized — the evidence does not support a single location</span>
    <span class="k">What possibly happened</span><span class="v">The IPsec tunnel&#39;s IKE/DPD keepalives failed, so every application behind the tunnel lost its private path. — the fault condition is confirmed; the underlying root cause is still under investigation.</span>
    <span class="k">Possible owner(s)</span><span class="v">NetOps</span>
    <span class="k">Why</span><span class="v" style="font-weight:400">named by the &#34;IPsec tunnel down — cloud private path&#34; hypothesis (confirmed)</span>
  </div>
  
  <div class="note"></div>
  
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Management summary</h2>
  <div class="mgmt">At 2026-07-12 18:00:00 UTC, One automated check detected a condition of “ipsec tunnel down — cloud private path” affecting lab-svc. The condition is ongoing (2h 00m elapsed). Synthetic path impact is confirmed; actual real-user impact was not confirmed because relevant real-traffic telemetry was insufficient. The fault condition is confirmed and the affected domain has been localized; the underlying root cause remains under investigation. Decision: Open incident — Customer impact and fault are confirmed by independent evidence; restoration workflow should begin. Escalation follows the policy thresholds stated in the decision section.</div>
  <div class="note">Confidence basis: independent confirmation across 1 evidence classes and 1 observers. Incident severity: Validation scenario — production severity not applicable; simulated severity reflects the injected condition only. <span style="color:#94a3b8">(evidence-peak severity: peak of the attached evidence, carried by ipsec tunnel status (2 crit of 2 anomalous observations); validation scenario — production severity not applicable)</span></div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Key facts</h2>
  <div class="kv">
    <span class="k">First observed</span><span class="v">2026-07-12 18:00:00 UTC</span>
    
    
    <span class="k">Duration</span><span class="v">2h 00m (elapsed — still active)</span>
    
    
    
    <span class="k">Root cause</span><span class="v">Not confirmed — possibly because of the IPsec tunnel&#39;s IKE/DPD keepalives failed, so every application behind the tunnel lost its private path.</span>
  </div>
</section>


<div class="pmh">2 · Impact</div>
<section>
