</section>


<div class="pmh">8 · Corrective actions</div>
<section>
  <h2>Immediate next actions</h2>
  <ol class="actions">
  <li><span class="pill red" style="font-size:9px">P1</span> <b>Check the tunnel&#39;s IKE_SA on the VPN gateway</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: IKE/child-SA state, last DPD result, and rekey timestamps from the gateway</div></li>
  <li><span class="pill red" style="font-size:9px">P1</span> <b>Inspect the most recent failed check transaction</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: DNS result, resolved IP, TCP status, TLS status, HTTP status, response time, and the failure stage</div></li>
  <li><span class="pill blue" style="font-size:9px">P2</span> <b>Compare real traffic, load-balancer target health and application errors during the incident window</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: request volume, completion rate, load-balancer target health, application error rate</div><div class="note">Escalate when: real-user impact, flow loss, or application errors corroborate the checks</div></li>
  <li><span class="pill blue" style="font-size:9px">P2</span> <b>Run the same check from an independent vantage (only prober-lab has reported this)</b> — owner: NOC<div class="note">Expected output: the same target&#39;s result from a second vantage — fails there too (target side) or only here (local side)</div></li>
  
  </ol>
  <div class="note">Durable corrective-action commitments (accountable owner, due date, success criteria, verification) are managed in the case's action register; a printed document is a status snapshot as of generation time. Validation scenario: this document makes no production corrective-action commitments.</div>
</section>


